Active, reactive, apparent and waveform power (@pe-complex-power: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electrical-power-engineering, #source "../sources/AC-Electrical-Circuit-Analysis-Fiore.lingua#r_0C4FYP5P0A5GQP13HAD8FTEEWK", #source "../sources/Introduction-to-Electric-Power-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_6JR10ZVGMZ7GT4RRK7734JQ7WD", #electrical-power-engineering "Power-factor-correction-geometry-loss-and-resonance.lingua#r_7PF3WW4CWYA2BBF4FPZ1YZTJ4M") { r_7ME7DSWC0ZMS4V97BTQGC5C323
**Read:** [AC Electrical Circuit Analysis — James M. Fiore](../sources/AC-Electrical-Circuit-Analysis-Fiore.lingua#r_0C4FYP5P0A5GQP13HAD8FTEEWK), complete AC power and power-factor chapters; [Introduction to Electric Power Systems — MIT 6.061](../sources/Introduction-to-Electric-Power-Systems-MIT.lingua#r_6JR10ZVGMZ7GT4RRK7734JQ7WD), chapter 2 in full.

For a single sinusoidal port using the declared RMS/passive convention, S = VI*, P = Re S, Q = Im S and |S| = V_rms I_rms. Derive the average and twice-frequency terms of instantaneous power. Reactive power describes reversible exchange within this sinusoidal model; it is not a separately consumed net energy analogous to resistive heat.

For P = 8 kW and Q = 6 kvar, apparent power is 10 kVA and displacement power factor 0.8. At fixed voltage, reducing unnecessary reactive current can reduce current-related losses and release capacity, but the resulting equipment/network interaction must be studied. A capacitor's presence alone does not prove acceptable voltage or harmonic behavior.

For distorted waveforms, active power remains the time average of v(t)i(t), while apparent power uses total RMS values. Fundamental displacement factor and true power factor then differ; a single fundamental Q does not summarize every distortion effect. Measure the waveform/bandwidth and use the actual applicable power definitions. Later harmonic and metrology Records connect those definitions to transformer heating, neutral current and instrument evidence.

**Continue:** [Power-factor correction, loss and resonance](Power-factor-correction-geometry-loss-and-resonance.lingua#r_7PF3WW4CWYA2BBF4FPZ1YZTJ4M).

